    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537186/lecturer-in-physiologyanatomy-in-the-school-of-biomedical-sciences": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Physiology/Anatomy in the School of Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Lecturer in Physiology/Anatomy in the School of Biomedical Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537186 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer in Physiology/Anatomy in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537186), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal. Applicants should have a Ph.D. and M.B.B.S or M.D. degree and be highly motivated in teaching and learning, with at least 3 years of demonstrated experience and excellence in the teaching of the physiology/anatomy discipline for medical, nursing, pharmacy, and biomedical sciences undergraduate and postgraduate degree programmes. Applicants should also have strong communication and organizational skills, the ability to work independently and as a team, and be able to multitask. Experience in teaching physiology, anatomy, biochemistry, or digital education in medicine is a plus. The appointee will be responsible for teaching, conducting tutorials and demonstrations, supporting curriculum design, and developing teaching materials, etc.  He/She will work closely with a team of colleagues dedicated to the development and delivery of innovative pedagogical approaches to improve student learning across several undergraduate and postgraduate degree programmes. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salary tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. together with a teaching statement. Review of applications will start from September 15, 2026 and continue until 31 October 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537186 Lecturer in Physiology/Anatomy in the School of Biomedical Sciences School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537186 Lecturer in Physiology/Anatomy in the School of Biomedical Sciences School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
