    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537175/assistant-it-manager-software-developer-at-the-rank-of-it-officer-it-technician": {
      "title": "Assistant IT Manager / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant IT Manager / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537175 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Clinical Medicine (23000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant IT Manager / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) in the School of Clinical Medicine (several posts) (Ref.: 537175) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a recognised Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline, and a minimum of 3 years of relevant post-qualification experience in the IT industry.  Experience in web applications, system maintenance/development that would automate administrative work processes and enhance workflow within the context of an educational institution would be an advantage.  Proficient in both written and spoken English and Chinese.  Fresh graduates who are highly motivated may also be considered for appointment at IT Technician rank. Applicants should have a strong sense of responsibility with good interpersonal skills, and be able to work well with our dynamic Teaching and Learning Team under a fast-paced environment.  They should possess profound knowledge in Frontend programming, such as React, Typescript, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP, and Backend Programming, such as Node.js and be proficient in relational databases like MySQL, Postgres DB, SQL Server, and Oracle. They should also have knowledge of DevOps methodologies, CI/CD pipelines, and Git version control.  Those with higher qualifications and/or richer experience may be considered for appointment as IT Officer. The appointees will be responsible for maintenance, enhancement and development of applications/systems for frontline operations in teaching and learning, including the Moodle and Panopto platforms, as well as IT support for different systems and events. On-the-job training will be provided.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or skills test. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536550) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until September 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537175 Assistant IT Manager / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) School of Clinical Medicine (23000) Sep 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537175 Assistant IT Manager / Software Developer (