    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537336/professor-associate-professor-assistant-professor-in-landscape-architecture-in-the-division-of-landscape-architecture-department-of-architecture": {
      "title": "Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Landscape Architecture in the Division of Landscape Architecture, Department of Architecture",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Architecture 1 Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Landscape Architecture in the Division of Landscape Architecture, Department of Architecture The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537336 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Architecture (01100) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Landscape Architecture in the Division of Landscape Architecture, Department of Architecture (Ref. 537336) , to commence on 1 September 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. We seek a productive and creative scholar whose research, teaching, and practice engages in critical dialogue with core concepts, histories, theories, and methods in the field of landscape architecture. Appointment will be made on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract. Exceptionally outstanding candidates for Professor/ Associate Professor may be considered for appointment on tenure terms. About the Division: The Division of Landscape Architecture offers an internationally recognized, rigorous, and dynamic research and teaching environment within the Department of Architecture at the University of Hong Kong. Staff members take an active part in shaping the Division’s culture through both teaching and administrative responsibilities in our undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. While we strive to continue to strengthen our regional leadership in the field of Landscape Architecture, we are actively developing international collaborations and building long-term relationships in greater Southeast Asia and beyond. More information about the Division and the Faculty of Architecture at HKU can be found at https://www.arch.hku.hk/programmes_/dla/ . Qualifications: Applicants should hold a terminal degree in Landscape Architecture and preference will be given to those holding professional qualifications and/or a Ph.D. in Landscape Architecture, or to those who have experience in award-winning professional or creative practice. They should demonstrate an emerging record of research, teaching, and design through their scholarship and creative work as evidenced by peer review and successful funding applications. As the Division continues to build regional and international links with academic institutions and innovators working at the intersection of landscape architecture, ecology, and technology, applicants who have of potential for building such partnerships will be favored. Responsibilities: The appointee is expected to pursue a productive and innovative research and design agenda in line with their area of expertise and in support of larger Division educational and scholarly aims. Teaching responsibilities may include core and elective seminars and design studio courses within our Bachelor and Master’s programs in landscape architecture. The appointee will also be encouraged to attract and supervise PhD students. Broadly, the successful candidate will help build and sustain our innovation in design research and help deliver innovative teaching and community engagement that builds on ongoing research and pedagogical initiatives within the Division. For enquiries about the position, please write to Professor Eunice Seng, Head of the Department of Architecture (e-mail: eseng@hku.hk). Compensation and Benefits: A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and professional leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. Application: The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online with the following: Statement of Interest (~2 pages) describing the applicant’s experience and suitability for the position and their future goals for research or creative practice, and teaching. Curriculum vitae Portfolio of Research and/or Creative Practice, and Teaching (< 30MB) Contact information of three senior academics familiar with the applicant’s teaching and research experience. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537336 Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Landscape Architecture in the Division of Landscape Architecture, Department of Architecture Department of Architecture (01100) Dec 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537336 Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Landscape Architecture in the Division of Landscape Architecture, Department of Architecture Department of Architecture (01100) Dec 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537368/temporary-senior-executive-assistant-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii": {
      "title": "Temporary Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Temporary Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537368 Work type: Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref: 537368), to commence on November 1, 2026 or as soon as possible thereafter, on full-time or part-time basis for a temporary term of 6 months. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree with at least 2-4 years of administrative experience, preferably in the tertiary education sector; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Putonghua); Strong sense of responsibility and be attentive to details; Good interpersonal, organisational, communication, and problem-solving skills; Ability to work independently and as part of a team; and Proficiency in IT especially in MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint with an intermediate level of artificial intelligence literacy. Applicants with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for the appointment of Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II). Responsibilities The appointee will provide a wide range of administrative and clerical support to the Student Team on undergraduate curricula, including handling admissions, student matters, day-to-day enquiries, and assisting in programme administration; providing general support to committees; supporting academic activities and events; and performing any other duties as assigned. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. Advertised: Sep 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537368 Temporary Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537368 Temporary Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
