    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537307/research-assistant-iii-several-posts-in-antibodyprotein-development": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in Antibody/Protein Development",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in Antibody/Protein Development The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537307 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in Antibody/Protein Development (Ref.:537307) We now invite applications for the captioned posts which focus on antibody and protein production and characterization, in the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine and the State Key Laboratory of Pharmaceutical Biotechnology Duties and Responsibilities Develop and validate innovative technologies for research, diagnostic or therapeutic applications, including antigens, antibodies and immune assays Assist in diverse molecular biology experiments, including PCR, Western blotting, cell culture, and DNA extraction Perform other duties as assigned 5.5 workday per week is required Requirements A Bachelor’s degree or above in Biology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Engineering, Biochemistry or a related discipline; preferably with experience in antibody screening and protein engineering Strong communication and collaboration skills, high motivation, and the ability to work under tight schedules Experience with animal experiments is an advantage For more information about our research directions, please visit our lab website: https://www.sklpb.hku.hk What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536447) need not re-apply. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from September 25, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537307 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in Antibody/Protein Development Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537307 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in Antibody/Protein Development Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
