    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537346/scientific-officer-holding-the-title-of-educational-psychologist-in-the-department-of-psychology": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Scientific Officer (holding the title of Educational Psychologist) in the Department of Psychology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537346 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychology (30200) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong We now invite applications for the captioned post. Scientific Officer (holding the title of Educational Psychologist) in the Department of Psychology (Ref.: 537346 ) (to commence in November 2026, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and totaling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability). Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will play a key role in a large-scale neurodiversity initiative project for primary schools in Hong Kong, under the Department of Psychology, Faculty of Social Sciences. The appointee will be responsible for the professional oversight and strategic implementation of the project, requiring specialised knowledge and independent professional judgement, with major tasks including: Devising and implementing a programme to foster a neurodiversity culture for primary school students Developing and implementing a school-wide support programme focused on developing a neurodiversity culture in schools Providing consultation and ongoing professional support to educators and parents to promote students’ well-being Organising and delivering training sessions and workshops for educators, parents, and students Consultation, coaching, and support for the multidisciplinary team Planning and implementing public education initiatives Preparing research reports and non-technical documents Performing any other duties as assigned Requirements The appointment will be offered based on the qualifications and experience of the applicant. The appointee should possess: A master's degree or higher in educational psychology or a related field eligible for clinical practice, along with at least three years of relevant work experience Strong analytical and organisational skills, with experience in managing research or community projects within psychology, social sciences, or related fields Excellent written and spoken communication skills in English and Chinese Experience in consultation and coaching for a multi-disciplinary team is preferred Relevant work experience in a school setting, project work, or an additional postgraduate diploma in education is preferred. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience, along with annual leave, medical benefits, and opportunities for professional development. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 30 September, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537346 Scientific Officer (holding the title of Educational Psychologist) in the Department of Psychology Department of Psychology (30200) Sep 30, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537346 Scientific Officer (holding the title of Educational Psychologist) in the Department of Psychology Department of Psychology (30200) Sep 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
