    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537392/research-assistant-professor-postdoctoral-fellow-in-the-faculty-of-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537392 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences We now invite applications for the captioned post, who will involve in the Jockey Club End-of-Life Community Care Project ( www.JCECC.hk ). Duties and Responsibilities Involve in the research team of the Project to work on research and evaluation studies in end-of-life care (EoLC). Duties and responsibilities include: Supervise a team of research staff on research and evaluation tasks in EoLC Perform advanced level of data analysis (quantitative and qualitative) Advance knowledge based on the data and disseminate it through peer-review journals, press conference or other means Draft reports and presentations relevant to the project Liaise with project collaborators and partners Mentor junior research staff Support and perform other duties as assigned Requirements Ph.D. degree in Social Work, Gerontology, Nursing, Counseling, Public Health, Psychology, Behavioral Health, Mental Health or a related discipline, preferably with clinical experiences in EoLC or gerontology care Good command of written and spoken Chinese (Cantonese) and English Ability to multi-task and work on a tight schedule to meet project deadlines Ability to work well independently and collaboratively as a team Ability to develop a body of high-quality publications in scholarly journals with global impact Proficiency in statistical software packages, including SPSS and R, for large and complex data analysis Proven knowledge and experience in undertaking research related to EoLC is advantageous Relevant post-doctoral work experience and an excellent track record of publications will be advantages Applicants with less experience or qualifications may be considered for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow What We Offer The appointment will commence from as soon as possible on temporary basis until June 30, 2027. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online, upload a covering letter and an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537392 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537392 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
