    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537235/senior-technical-officer-in-the-hku-kadoorie-centre-ref-537235": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior Technical Officer in the HKU Kadoorie Centre (Ref.: 537235) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537235 Work type: Full-time Department: HKU Kadoorie Centre (53000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer in the HKU Kadoorie Centre (Ref.: 537235) Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Technical Officer in the HKU Kadoorie Centre (Ref.: 537235), to commence as soon as possible, on a two years fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. The HKU Kadoorie Centre Founded in the mid-1980s through the visionary philanthropy of Sir Horace Kadoorie and Lord Lawrence Kadoorie, the HKU Kadoorie Centre is situated near Shek Kong in Hong Kong’s New Territories. The Centre takes a cross-disciplinary approach to address urgent challenges in agriculture, energy systems, water resources, nature conservation, and more. By integrating scientific knowledge at both regional and global levels, the Centre drives technological innovation for sustainability. In addition to supporting scholars and students from the University, the Centre places a strong emphasis on collaborative innovation with local and international academic communities, advancing interdisciplinary solutions to complex global challenges. The Role The HKU Kadoorie Centre invites applications for the position of Senior Technical Officer in the area of Food-Energy-Water Systems at the Centre. Qualifications and Requirements The minimum academic requirement is a bachelor’s degree, with three to five years of relevant work experience. Preference will be given to candidates with a higher degree. Applicants should also have extensive experience in one or more of the following areas: Protected agriculture, precision farming, including greenhouse energy and environment management Sustainable materials and technologies, including but not limited to renewable energy materials and systems, solar management materials and systems, as well as the scale manufacturing of materials Experts from other technological areas in sustainability, renewable technology, and environmental technology are also welcome to apply. Enquiries about the post may be sent to Prof. X. Yin at xbyin@hku.hk . Other requirements include strong written and verbal communication skills; a strong record of technical excellence; the ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team; and experience in project coordination and management. The appointee will be expected to provide technical and operational support for programmes and outreach activities conducted at the Kadoorie Centre. Duties may include preparing and setting up equipment and facilities, coordinating on-site technical arrangements, providing demonstrations and operational guidance, and ensuring that activities are conducted safely and smoothly. The appointee will also liaise with internal and external parties and provide logistical support as required. Experience in supporting student activities, workshops or public engagement programmes would be an advantage. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online, together with an up-to-date CV, a cover letter detailing experience and interests, and contact information for at least three referees. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 15, 2025 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537235 Senior Technical Officer in the HKU Kadoorie Centre (Ref.: 537235) HKU Kadoorie Centre (53000) Oct 15, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537235 Senior Technical Officer in the HKU Kadoorie Centre (Ref.: 537235) HKU Kadoorie Centre (53000) Oct 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537292/research-nurse-at-the-rank-of-nurse": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Categories Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537292 Work type: Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Hong Kong Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 537292) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies.  HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession. HKU-CTC’s Phase 1 Clinical Trials Unit (Phase 1 Unit) is a professional clinical trials facility located at the Queen Mary Hospital and dedicated to conducting phase 1 and early phase clinical trials.  We are seeking a high calibre talent who have the passion in promoting healthcare advancement through practising clinical research to join our Phase 1 Unit as a Research Nurse. Main Responsibilities: Be responsible to clinical trial coordination and operations; Conduct study planning and management; Recruit trial volunteers; Execute study procedures, data collection and documents management, medical emergency management, facilities management and quality management; Communicate with research teams and internal/external collaborators; and Perform other duties as assigned. Require to work outside normal business days or hours occasionally. Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Nursing; Registered with the Nursing Council of Hong Kong; A minimum of 1 year’s nursing experience is preferred; Holder of a Basic Life Support (BLS) / Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support (ACLS) certificate and a venipuncture certificate is an advantage; Experience in clinical trial operations and basic knowledge in Good Clinical Practice are added advantages; Experience in utilization of electronic devices (e.g., tablets, computers) for efficient and accurate clinical data capture are added advantages; Good interpersonal and communication skills; Good coordination and problem-solving skills, and commitment to quality and compliance; Detail-minded, able to multitask, and self-motivated; and Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Both Cantonese & Mandarin). The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Appointment on 2-year fixed term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Application Procedure: The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will begin from October 1, 2026 and continue until October 16, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537292 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Oct 16, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537292 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Oct 16, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537319/it-technician-holding-the-functional-title-of-system-specialist-it-technologist-2-posts": {
      "title": "IT Technician (holding the functional title of System Specialist/ IT Technologist) (2 Posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 IT Technician (holding the functional title of System Specialist/ IT Technologist) (2 Posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537319 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as IT Technician (holding the functional title of System Specialist / IT Technologist ) (2 Posts) in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537319) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) With the establishment of the School of Computing and Data Science, we are seeking high-calibre team members to support the School’s strategic initiatives and growing academic development of taught postgraduate degree programme across the following key functional areas: 1. General IT, AV & Infrastructure Support 2. Systems Development & Infrastructure Support The Role The appointees will support the development, maintenance, and enhancement of the Master Programme Office's (MPO) internal systems, IT infrastructure, and digitalisation and workflow automation initiatives. Major responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Core responsibilities Perform routine system updates, security patches, user account management, and network configuration to maintain a secure and efficient IT environment. Provide timely and professional IT support to staff and students on hardware, software, networks, user accounts, printing, office applications, and other general IT services. Maintain and support server infrastructure, including virtualization platforms such as VMware and Hyper-V, high-availability configurations such as failover clusters, server operating systems, monitoring, backup, and routine maintenance. Perform other duties as assigned in support of MPO operations and programme activities. General IT, AV & Infrastructure Support Support classroom teaching and programme activities, including setup, operation, and troubleshooting of computers, AV systems, presentation equipment, e-learning tools, and other teaching technologies. Manage, maintain, install, configure, and troubleshoot computing, audiovisual, teaching, and office IT facilities across Windows and other operating system platforms. Systems Development & Infrastructure Support Assist in designing, developing, enhancing, and maintaining in-house systems, websites, web applications, and internal tools. Working hours may occasionally include weekday evenings (until 7:30 PM) and weekends, to accommodate teaching schedules. Qualifications and Qualities Core requirements A recognised Bachelor’s degree/ Higher Diploma or above in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline. Relevant experience in IT support, system administration, infrastructure support, or systems development. Able to perform basic network configuration and troubleshooting, including IP addressing, DNS, DHCP, subnetting, and network connectivity issues. Experience in providing technical support for hardware, software, network, printing, office applications, and general IT services. Experience or knowledge in server infrastructure support, including server operating systems, monitoring, backup, routine maintenance, and troubleshooting. Familiarity with virtualization platforms such as VMware and Hyper-V, and high-availability technologies such as failover clustering, would be an advantage. Able to work independently and as part of a team, with a responsible and service-oriented attitude. Good troubleshooting, problem-solving, communication, and customer service skills. General IT, AV & Infrastructure Support Hands-on experience in setting up, operating, maintaining, and troubleshooting computers, AV systems, presentation equipment, and office tools. Knowledge of computing, audiovisual, teaching, and office IT facilities, including installation, configuration, maintenance, and troubleshooting. Systems Development & Infrastructure Support Experience in developing or maintaining websites, web applications, in-house systems, or internal tools. Knowledge of web development technologies, databases, scripting, or programming languages is required. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 17, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 17, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537319 IT Technician (holding the functional title of System Specialist/ IT Technologist) (2 Posts) School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Oct 17, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537319 IT Technician (holding the functional title of System Specialist/ IT Technologist) (2 Posts) School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Oct 17, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
