      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Research Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537383 Work type: Full-time Department: Jao Tsung-I Petite Ecole (45600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Jao Tsung-I Petite Ecole (to commence as soon as possible, on a 2 years fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in an Arts discipline plus at least 2 years’ working experience. Those with an advanced degree in art history, museum studies or cultural studies, and experience in exhibition-related work would have an advantage. They should also have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese including Putonghua, as well as strong organizational and communication skills, and proven design experience. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite, especially Illustrator and Photoshop, is required. The appointee will be responsible for assisting with research on Chinese art, organizing exhibitions, and performing other duties as assigned. The appointee will report to the Deputy Director. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical/dental benefits. The University thanks applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted applicants will be notified of the application result. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of application will start as soon as possible and continue until Oct 20, 2026 