    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537405/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537405 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-Doctoral Fellow in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537405), to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Doctoral degree in statistics, biostatistics, computer science, psychiatry, psychology or a related discipline. They should be familiar with programming languages such as R or Python and have a good command of written and spoken English. Those with expertise in MRI imaging analysis and neuroscience in clinical population, especially in psychiatry research will be preferred. The appointee will work on multiple projects on psychiatry research particularly focusing on MRI imaging and neuroscience. The appointee will work in a flexible environment, and have a chance to collaborate with health science, computer science and neuroscience experts.  For further enquiries about the duties of the post and/or the project, please contact Prof. Sherry Chan (kwsherry@hku.hk) A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start on October 02, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
