    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537333/senior-research-assistantresearch-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537333 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychology (30200) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Psychology (Ref.: 537333) Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Psychology (Ref.: 537333) to commence on October 5, 2026 or as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should have a Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, or a related discipline. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese); strong communication skills; basic knowledge in using statistical software such as SPSS and R; be self-motivated, responsible and able to work independently and as a team. Those with experience in working with children/adolescents are preferred. Applicants for the senior research assistant position are expected to have prior experience in managing research projects. The appointee will work on various projects related to children’s and adolescents’ mathematics and science learning. He/she will be responsible for literature review, preparation of assessment materials, liaise with external parties, coordination of research activities, conducting assessments with children and adolescents, supervision of research interns, data processing, and other research-related duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 5, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 5, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537333 Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II Department of Psychology (30200) Oct 5, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537333 Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II Department of Psychology (30200) Oct 5, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537339/executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537339 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) (Ref.: 537339) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) About Us Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) is an academic research-support centre embracing multi-omics and big data biomedical research under the LKS Faculty of Medicine.  CPOS core laboratories host state-of-the-art omics technology platforms with sophisticated equipment supported by our over 70 dedicated and trained members.  Welcome to visit us https://cpos.hku.hk to explore more. The Role Assist with daily office operations, including procurement, payments, reimbursements, and invoicing Manage and maintain databases, ensuring accuracy and consistency Handle service and payment enquiries from internal and external parties Provide customer service and support through effective written and verbal communication Support events, activities, and social media administration Perform various clerical and administrative tasks, such as filing, data entry, and correspondence management Carry out other duties as assigned Qualifications and Qualities Bachelor’s Degree/Diploma At least 1-2 years of relevant work experience Proficiency in advanced IT applications, including MS Office, particularly Excel Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese Good organizational and interpersonal skills Strong sense of responsibility, a fast learner, highly motivated and attentive to details A good team player with the ability to work independently Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537339 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537339 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537352/student-advising-officer-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537352 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Careers and Employability of the Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref.: 537352) (to commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefit scheme at 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance). We are seeking a motivated and proactive professional to oversee the planning and administration of the STEM Internship Scheme, funded by the Innovation and Technology Commission (ITC). The role focuses on promoting high-quality STEM-related internship opportunities, building partnerships with employers, and connecting students with meaningful industry experiences. The appointee will be responsible for the below duties: Coordinate the administration and day-to-day implementation of the STEM Internship Scheme, ensuring compliance with funding guidelines and programme requirements. Support the management of job applications, student vetting, scheme monitoring, and system administration. Liaise with external and internal stakeholders, including ITC, employers, faculty members, and students, on internship-related applications, documentation, approvals, and enquiries. Collect stakeholder feedback and provide advice to students on internship opportunities, application processes, and internship preparation. Support budget administration, financial reporting, and the processing of employer and student reimbursements and allowances. Assist in the development and enhancement of internship-related initiatives and services for students. Provide guidance to junior staff and undertake other duties as assigned in support of the team’s priorities. Applicants should possess: University degree with at least five years of work experience, preferably in project management or career services within tertiary institutions and/or large corporations. Familiarity with government-funded or university-wide programmes would be an asset. Experience in employer outreach, partnership development, or stakeholder engagement is desirable. Strong analytical mindset towards process enhancement and service improvement. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with a wide range of stakeholders. Good knowledge of the local employment market and awareness of emerging industry trends. An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Proficiency in Microsoft Office and experience in webpage design and social media marketing is an advantage. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a written test and interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until September 25, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537355/executive-officer-in-the-student-inclusion-and-support-of-centre-of-development-and-resources-for-students-cedars": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Officer in the Student Inclusion and Support of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537355 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the Student Inclusion and Support of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref.: 537355) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefit scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Renewal of contract is subject to the availability of project funding and mutual agreement.) The Role assist in the development, rollout, daily maintenance, and continuous improvement of hall admission systems, hostel management platforms, and related databases; organize, clean, validate, and standardize datasets, and develop guidelines for data standardization and shared-drive management; apply statistical methods and data analysis to support technology integration, evidence-based planning, and process improvement; conduct regular data audits, checks, and procedural reviews to ensure data accuracy, compliance, and operational quality; provide frontline user support, troubleshoot system and operational issues, and handle enquiries from site office staff and residential stakeholders; assist in conducting training workshops and preparing user manuals, operational guidelines, and system documentation to support smooth adoption of policies and platforms; liaise with University departments, residence management offices, and relevant residential stakeholders on housing operations and system-related matters; assist in coordinating residential initiatives, including residential education and housing partnerships, and support maintenance of websites, online resources, reports, and presentations; and perform any other duties as assigned by supervisor. Qualifications and Qualities a Bachelor's degree, preferably in Information Management, Statistics, Business Operations, Social Sciences, or a related discipline, with at least 3 to 5 years' relevant post-qualification experience; relevant experience in database management systems (DBMS), system implementation, quality assurance, data management, process improvement, or higher education/student housing administration; strong analytical ability and experience in organizing, validating, and analysing complex datasets; strong proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications, including Microsoft Copilot, workflow automation tools, VBA and SQL; experience in Power BI, AI solutions, and visual design tools such as Canva or Adobe Creative Suite would be an advantage; the ability to prepare user guides, conduct training workshops, provide user support, and communicate complex technical concepts effectively to non-technical users and stakeholders; excellent written and spoken English and Chinese (including native fluency in Cantonese), strong interpersonal and communication skills, and a positive, proactive, service-oriented attitude with the ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537400/assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537400 Work type: Full-time Department: Technology Transfer Office (99110) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Technology Transfer Office (Ref.:537400) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Key Responsibilities: Assist in the administration and coordination of the ITC-funded Research, Academic and Industry Sectors One-plus Scheme (RAISe+) Scheme under the direction of the program manager. Facilitate RAISe+ project administration including progress monitoring, compliance verification, reporting requirements. Support other funded innovation projects as needed. Organize and manage events, workshops, and training sessions to foster innovation and knowledge exchange. Support collaboration among faculty, industry partners, venture funders, and government officials. Assist with company secretarial and administrative tasks, including record-keeping and ensuring compliance. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities: A Bachelor’s degree or above with at least 3 years of relevant experience in project management, innovation, or technology transfer. Experience in tertiary education institutions or research-intensive environments preferred. Knowledge of company secretarial practices, including corporate governance and statutory filings, is an advantage. Strong organizational and project management skills; ability to manage multiple tasks independently. Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Putonghua). Proficient in Microsoft Office and financial/project management systems. Proactive, detail-oriented, and results-driven, with a passion for innovation and technology. Strong interpersonal and networking skills to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders. Knowledge of intellectual property management, commercialization, or funding schemes (e.g., RAISe+) is an advantage. Information about the Office can be obtained at https://rise.hku.hk/en . Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref: 534620) need not re-apply. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 19, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537400 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) Technology Transfer Office (99110) Oct 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537400 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive 