    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537372/tenuretrack-clinical-professor": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Clinical Professor",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537372 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Clinical Professor in Breast Surgery in the Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537372), to commence as soon as possible, on a four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second four-year fixed-term contract.  Exceptionally outstanding candidates may be considered for appointment on tenure terms. Applicants should possess a specialist qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong, a higher professional qualification of Specialty Fellowship in Surgery of The College of Surgeons of Hong Kong or equivalent, and other relevant higher academic qualifications (e.g., MD, MS, PhD).  They should be specialized surgeons of seniority, with demonstrated clinical excellence in the broad field of Breast Surgery.  They should also have a distinguished and sustained record of high-quality impactful research, as indicated by publications and competitive grants; and have achieved international recognition for scholarship and professional expertise.  In addition, applicants should have a strong commitment to, and evidence of, excellence in teaching, curriculum development, capacity building, mentoring early career researchers and supervision at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels.  Preference will be given to those with demonstrated administrative leadership and management experience in universities or healthcare settings.  Direct communication with patients is required and the languages employed are Cantonese, Putonghua and English. The appointee will take up a key role in achieving the highest standard of quality in all aspects of teaching, research, clinical service and administration of the Department; fostering academic collaboration within and outside the Faculty/University; as well as pursuing new strategic directions for the further development of the Department, Faculty and University.  In addition, he/she may be required to assist in the development of the HKU-Shenzhen Hospital, and travelling to Shenzhen may therefore be necessary.  Further information about the Department can be obtained at http://www.surgery.hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidate.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload (a) an executive summary describing the most outstanding accomplishments and qualifications; (b) a C.V. and a publication list highlighting the best papers; and (c) a 1-page description of the future research and career plan.   Review of applications will start on November 19, 2026 and continue until December 19, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 19, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537372 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Dec 19, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537372 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Dec 19, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537373/clinical-associate-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate Professor of Practice",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clinical Associate Professor of Practice The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537373 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Clinical Associate Professor of Practice in Otorhinolaryngology in the Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537373), to commence as soon as possible on a four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong and a higher professional qualification of Fellowship in Otorhinolaryngology of The Hong Kong College of Otorhinolaryngologists or equivalent.  They should be specialized otorhinolaryngologists of seniority and be clinically competent in the field.  They should have a strong commitment to, and demonstrated excellence in, teaching medical students and training residents, and the capacity to contribute to undergraduate curriculum development.  Good achievements in research and publications in the field would be an advantage.  Direct communication with patients is required and the languages employed are Cantonese, Putonghua and English. The appointee will teach, organize and develop undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, provide clinical service and patient care at the University's teaching hospitals, conduct research, and contribute to administrative duties in the Department and the Faculty.  In addition, he/she may be required to assist in the development of the HKU-Shenzhen Hospital, and travelling to Shenzhen may therefore be necessary.  Further information about the Department can be obtained at http://www.surgery.hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidate.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload (a) an executive summary describing the most outstanding accomplishments and qualifications; (b) a C.V. and a publication list highlighting the best papers; and (c) a 1-page description of the future career and research plan.  Review of applications will start on November 19, 2026 and continue until December 19, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 19, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537373 Clinical Associate Professor of Practice Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Dec 19, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537373 Clinical Associate Professor of Practice Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Dec 