    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537415/fractional-clinical-associate-professorclinical-assistant-professor-in-implant-dentistry": {
      "title": "Fractional Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Implant Dentistry",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Fractional Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Implant Dentistry The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537415 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Non-Tenure Track Fractional Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Implant Dentistry of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537415), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to four-year fixed-term (50% fractional) basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. The Faculty of Dentistry is the only dental school in Hong Kong, China and the only one in China that uses English as the medium of instruction.  The high quality of the Faculty’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, research excellence, knowledge exchange (KE) and clinical/professional services have attained global recognition, as evidenced by the Faculty’s global rankings among the top three by the QS World University Rankings by Subject for ten out of the past twelve years (2015-2026).  The Faculty’s strategic research themes include AI+ & Precision Dentistry, Regenerative Dentistry, Global Oral Health, and Oral Ecosystem & One Health.  The Faculty also plays important roles in public and professional education through its KE activities and Global Education Hub for Oral Healthcare Professionals (GEHOHP), translational research & innovation via its Global Hub for Future Dentistry (GHFD) in collaboration with HKU Techno-Entrepreneurship Core and Hong Kong Science & Technology Parks Corporation, and enhancement of its global impacts through proactive engagement, networking and partnership. Applicants should demonstrate excellence in clinical care, research and teaching in the field of Implant Dentistry on top of sound knowledge and training in Periodontology. They are expected to work collaboratively in a dynamic and diverse environment, develop a competitive research portfolio, and contribute to the curricula available at the undergraduate and postgraduate level. Ability to partake undergraduate Periodontology teaching / education and fluency in spoken and written English are essential. For appointment as Clinical Associate Professor , applicants should possess a Dental Bachelor's degree or equivalent, a clinical specialist qualification or equivalent status in Implant Dentistry, Prosthodontics or Periodontology, advanced training or clinical experience in Implant Dentistry, and a Ph.D. degree or equivalent.  They should also have (i) proven ability for quality research, high quality publications in international journals, and evidence of local and regional recognition for scholarship and professional expertise; (ii) demonstrated ability in undergraduate and postgraduate education, clinical practice and research; (iii) demonstrated clinical expertise; (iv) demonstrated participation in Faculty and University affairs; and (v) demonstrated ability in KE activities, and leadership in professional education programmes or community engagement. For appointment as Clinical Assistant Professor , applicants should possess a Dental Bachelor’s degree or equivalent, a Master of Dental Surgery degree or equivalent in Implant Dentistry, Prosthodontics or Periodontology, and advanced training or clinical experience in Implant Dentistry.  They should also have (i) ability in undergraduate and postgraduate clinical teaching and practice; (ii) potential for and interest in research; (iii) proven ability in clinical excellence; (iv) ability and willingness to participate in Faculty affairs; and (v) active participation in KE activities. The appointee will engage in clinical and didactic teaching in Implant Dentistry at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, supervise research projects, be expected to develop their own line of research, and participate in the clinical and administrative duties of the Faculty. Information about the Faculty can be obtained at http://facdent.hku.hk/ .  For general enquiries, please contact Professor L.J. Jin, Dean of the Faculty of Dentistry at ljjin@hku.hk .  For information about the post, please contact Professor W.K. Leung, Chief, Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry, at ewkleung@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The successful candidate is required to obtain a valid registration with the Dental Council of Hong Kong.  (Note: Applicants who do not hold a local dental license must fulfil the essential requirements under the laws of a jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, China, to be eligible for Limited Registration.  For details, please refer to the Dental Council of Hong Kong’s website at https://www.dchk.org.hk/en/registration/part_III.html .) The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload a cover letter, an up-to-date C.V., a research statement and a teaching statement.  They should also indicate clearly which post (i.e. Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Assistant Professor) they wish to be considered for and please note that the final decision will be made by the University.  Closes October 17, 2026 . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 17, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537415 Fractional Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Implant Dentistry Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 17, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537415 Fractional Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Implant Dentistry Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 17, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537382/assistant-research-officer-senior-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Officer / Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Assistant Research Officer / Senior Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537382 Work type: Full-time Department: Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for the position of Assistant Research Officer / Senior Research Assistant (carrying the functional title of Project Manager) at the Social Sciences Research Centre (SSRC) within the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537382), to commence as soon as possible. The appointment is on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will provide a full spectrum of support to the research activities of the SSRC in various areas, including project management; project implementation and coordination; oversee data collection and management; liaise with different stakeholders and institutions; facilitate the collection of data; supervise junior research support staff; survey design and implementation; data cleaning and analysis; grant proposal preparation; academic paper and policy report writing; training and event organisation; as well as performing any other duties as assigned by the senior management team of the Centre. Requirements a Master’s degree or above in a Social Sciences discipline, preferably in project management, data analysis or a related field; a PhD degree will be an advantage; at least 2 years’ relevant work experience, including experience supervising junior research staff or student helpers; hands-on experience in survey research, including questionnaire design, sampling, fieldwork coordination and data quality control; a track record of grant proposal preparation and of writing academic papers or policy reports for research or government audiences; experience in project budgeting, procurement and progress reporting to funders, and in liaising with external partners, funders and government or NGO stakeholders; strong quantitative skills, including experience with statistical software such as R, SAS or Stata, and the ability to manage and analyse large and complex datasets; familiarity with research ethics review procedures and with personal data privacy requirements applicable to human-subject research data; an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; the ability to communicate fluently in Cantonese is essential, and a working command of Putonghua is expected; excellent organisational, time-management and problem-solving skills, with the ability to handle multiple tasks to tight deadlines; and the ability to effectively engage with external stakeholders, including academics, social service groups, and policymakers; strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work well with people from diverse backgrounds; mature and meticulous in handling matters. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue un til October 31, 2026 , o r until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537382 Assistant Research Officer / Senior Research Assistant Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537382 Assistant Research Officer / Senior Research Assistant Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537414/parttime-research-assistant-i-senior-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537414 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Centre for Applied English Studies (05300) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant in the Centre for Applied English Studies (CAES) (to commence as soon as possible, on a six-month temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) We are seeking a dedicated Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant to join the dynamic team at the Communication-intensive Courses (CiC) at The University of Hong Kong. In this role, the appointee will assist the investigators in managing and processing research data, reviewing relevant literature, analyzing and reporting findings, and supporting the project leader in various research activities related to the development of Communication-intensive Courses. He/She is expected to work 20-25 hours per week. Applicants should have: (i) a Master’s degree or higher in Education, Communication, Psychology, Social Sciences, or a related discipline; (ii) at least 2 years’ relevant post-qualification work experience, preferably in the higher education sector; (iii) an excellent command of written and spoken English, with proficiency in Cantonese and Mandarin preferred; (iv) experience in analysing both quantitative and qualitative data, with strong expertise in qualitative research methodologies; (v) a proactive, outgoing, and self-motivated approach, with strong organisational skills; (vi) the ability to work both independently and collaboratively as an effective team player; and (vii) familiarity with data analysis software, such as MAXQDA and NVivo, as well as MS Office applications, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. This is an exciting opportunity to work in a supportive environment that values innovation, teamwork, and professional growth. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Please visit https://cics.hku.hk for more information about CiC. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers website (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload a covering letter and an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until Oct 30, 202 6 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier . The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expressly encourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537414 Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant Centre for Applied English Studies (05300) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537414 Part-time Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant Centre for Applied English Studies (05300) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
