    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537325/senior-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-i-in-the-school-of-future-media": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the School of Future Media",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the School of Future Media The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537325 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Future Media (31200) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for the appointment as Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the School of Future Media (SFM) (Ref.: 537325) to commence on as soon as possible, on two-year fixed term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal based on satisfactory performance and operational needs. The appointee will be responsible for supporting the administrative tasks, event logistics and programme management of the SFM, with major duties including: • Supporting administrative duties for special initiatives and projects under the SFM; • Assisting in the planning, organisation and execution of publicity events and enrichment activities, such as student ambassador scheme, Information Day, alumni gathering, summer programmes, talks, seminars and workshops, etc; • Coordinating tasks with external and internal units; and • Performing any duties as assigned by the School Director The appointee may be required to work overtime as and when necessary. Applicants should have a Bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years of administrative experience, preferably in the tertiary education sector. Fluency in English and Chinese (including Putonghua) is required. They should have good written and oral communication skills as well as organisational skills, the ability to work independently and under pressure, and proficiency in IT such as Microsoft Word, Excel and Powerpoint. They should also be self-motivated, and be able to effectively interact with people from diverse cultures. Experience in programme administration or event planning is a definite advantage. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 25, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537325 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Sep 25, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537325 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Sep 25, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
