    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537379/senior-research-assistantresearch-assistant-iii-in-the-department-of-social-work-and-social-administration": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537379 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Applicants are invited for the position of Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (Ref.:537379), to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in Social Work, Psychology, Social Sciences, or other related disciplines with three years’ post-qualification experience; or a Master’s degree in the above fields with one year’s post-qualification experience. They should have high proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese), skills in analytical valuation and generation of practical solutions, and the ability to work independently and as a team player. Those with post qualification work experience in social sciences research projects and knowledge of data analysis are highly preferred. The appointees will join the JC JoyAge Project to assist the Project Director and the Project Managers in managing, coordinating, and implementing research activities for elderly mental health services, overseeing data collection, drafting reports, and performing other relevant tasks assigned. Occasional support for the Project’s publicity events is expected. The appointees will have ample opportunities to work with Clinical Psychologists, Social Workers, other mental health professionals, and various stakeholders in the local community. Applicants with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered Research Assistant I/II. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV, a cover letter stating their background, and the contact information of one referee. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 30 November 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. For more information about the project, please visit the website: https://jcjoyage.hk/ . Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
