    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537411/technical-manager-i-ii-several-posts": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Technical Manager I / II (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537411 Work type: Full-time Department: Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (66065) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Technical Manager I / II (several posts) in the Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (Ref.: 537411) We are seeking dedicated candidates for the position of Technical Manager I / II to manage a diverse range of facilities, including academic, teaching, and research facilities, as well as residential buildings. The role encompasses responsibilities ranging from overseeing routine building maintenance and security operations to managing renovation projects and large-scale facilities upgrade initiatives. The Role The appointees will oversee the maintenance and management of electrical, mechanical, and building services systems in academic buildings. Key responsibilities include: Leading and supervising maintenance teams to ensure timely and efficient service delivery; Developing and implementing preventive maintenance and asset management strategies; Preparing budgets and cost estimates for maintenance and system upgrade projects; Coordinating with internal departments and external contractors to uphold safety, quality, and compliance standards; Conducting regular inspections and assessments to identify potential hazards and implement prompt corrective actions; and Ensuring adherence to safety regulations and environmental standards. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Building Services Engineering, or related disciplines; A minimum of 10 years’ professional experience in facilities management, with at least 6 to 8 years’ supervisory experience in the higher education sector, hospitals or non-governmental organizations; A valid Construction Industry Safety Training Certificate (Green Card) issued in accordance with Chapter 59 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (i.e. by attending the relevant safety training courses which are recognized by the Commissioner for Labour) or equivalent; Proficiency in MS Office applications, AutoCAD and hands-on experience with computer-aided facilities management (CAFM) system; Strong leadership and team management capabilities; Excellent problem-solving and organizational skills; Effective communication and interpersonal skills; and Ability to work under pressure and manage multiple tasks efficiently. Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Technical Manager II. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 8, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537412/technical-manager-i": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Technical Manager I The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537412 Work type: Full-time Department: Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (66065) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Technical Manager I in the Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (Ref.: 537412) We are seeking a dedicated and experienced candidate for the position of Technical Manager I to oversee the maintenance of our sloping landscapes and tree population. The Role The appointee will play a vital role in ensuring the safety, functionality, and aesthetic appeal of our campus grounds. Key responsibilities include: Overseeing the maintenance and management of slopes and trees across the campus, ensuring safety and compliance with environmental standards; Developing, implementing, and monitoring preventive maintenance programs for slope stabilization and tree health; Managing in-house staff and contractors to ensure high standards of work performance; Preparing budgets and cost estimates for projects related to slope and tree management; Conducting regular inspections and assessments to identify potential hazards and implement prompt corrective actions; Liaising with university departments, contractors, and external agencies as necessary; and Promoting and implementing sustainable practices in all aspects of work. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, Environmental Science, or related disciplines; At least 10 years’ relevant experience working in landscaping or in a similar role, preferably within an educational institution or large-scale organization; Corporate membership of HKIE or equivalent professional bodies; A valid Construction Industry Safety Training Certificate (Green Card) issued in accordance with Chapter 59 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (i.e. by attending the relevant safety training courses which are recognized by the Commissioner for Labour) or equivalent; Extensive knowledge of slope stabilization and tree management techniques; Strong leadership and team management skills; Excellent problem-solving, decision-making, and organizational abilities; Solid understanding of safety regulations and environmental standards; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 8, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537412 Technical Manager I Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (66065) Oct 8, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537412 Technical Manager I Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (66065) Oct 8, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
