    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537413/facilities-officer-holding-the-functional-title-of-assistant-engineer-several-posts": {
      "title": "Facilities Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Engineer) (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Facilities Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Engineer) (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537413 Work type: Full-time Department: Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (66065) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Facilities Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Engineer) (several posts) in the Maintenance and Operations Unit of the Estates Office (Ref.: 537413) We are seeking dedicated candidates for the position of Facilities Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Engineer) to join the Estates Office. The Role The appointees will be responsible for routine building maintenance, improvement works and alteration works in all aspects, particularly for academic and laboratory buildings, tendering process, site progress monitoring, supervision of and liaison with contractors, follow-up on service agreements and certificate renewals, and communication with the user departments / internal teams / external consultants to ensure that works are executed in order with qualified services.  They may be required to work shifts, overtime and on public holidays, subject to prior arrangements; and act as an emergency team coordinator outside regular office hours. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A Bachelor’s degree in Building Services Engineering (Electrical & Mechanical), Building Surveying, Real Estate, Facilities Management, Property Management, Building Services or related disciplines; OR a relevant diploma with 5 years’ experience; A valid Construction Industry Safety Training Certificate (Green Card) issued in accordance with Chapter 59 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (i.e. by attending the relevant safety training courses which are recognized by the Commissioner for Labour) or equivalent; Proficiency in MS Office applications, AutoCAD, and hands-on experience with  computer-aided facilities management (CAFM) system; and Possession of a valid Certificate of Registration of Electrical Worker (Grade A or above) would be an advantage. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.   Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 8, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
