    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537366/physiotherapist-ii": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Physiotherapist II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537366 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Physiotherapist II in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537366) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in Physiotherapy, and be registered with a valid Practicing Certificate from the Physiotherapists Board of Hong Kong. Relevant experience and/or interest in clinical research, project coordination, or working in non-governmental organisations (NGOs) or with individuals with disabilities will be highly preferred. Candidates should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including fluency in Cantonese).  They should demonstrate strong communication and organizational skills, with the capability to work independently, multitask, and meet strict deadlines. They should also be attentive to details, self-motivated, and highly responsible. The appointee will work for the “Jockey Club Health Programme for Adult Persons with Disabilities” under the supervision of Professor Kelvin Wang. He/She will work closely with internal and external parties to implement the project, focusing on providing physiotherapy support (i.e. conduct physical assessments, design and implement exercise plans for persons with disabilities). He/She will also support project execution and coordination, and perform other related duties as assigned by supervisors. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start October 6, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537366 Physiotherapist II School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537366 Physiotherapist II School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
