    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537446/assistant-registrar": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Assistant Registrar The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537446 Work type: Full-time Department: Academic Support and Examinations Section of the Registry (60392) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Assistant Registrar in the Academic Support and Examinations Section of the Registry (Ref.: 537446) The Role The appointee will lead the Academic Services Office to oversee matters related to the processing and distribution of University official documents, e.g. degree certificates, transcripts, testimonials, etc.; provision of academic support services to students and  alumni; development of the Academic Certificate Verification Platform (ACVP) Blockchain project; provide administrative support by acting as Secretary for a number of University committees; and perform any other duties as assigned by the supervisors.  He/She may be required to work outside normal office hours and on weekends. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess a good Bachelor's degree with at least 10 years' work experience at supervisory level, preferably in tertiary institutions.  They should have an excellent organisational, interpersonal, communication and problem-solving skills; ability to multitask under pressure with a high level of independence and self-motivation; a strong sense of responsibility; and an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua).  They should also possess a good record of policy formulation and implementation, good IT knowledge, committee secretaryship, and staff management experience. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a full-time fixed-term contract for two years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 16, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Advertised: Sep 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
