    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537474/manager-emba-marketing-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Manager, EMBA Marketing (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537474 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Manager, EMBA Marketing (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref: 537474) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should hold a bachelor’s degree and possess at least 5 years of proven experience in brand building, marketing campaign management, digital marketing, and organizing promotional events. Prior work experience in the higher education field is an advantage. Candidates must be high-calibre individuals capable of working independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment, with the ability to effectively manage multiple tasks and prioritize ad hoc requests. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), be detail-oriented, and possess strong communication and problem-solving skills.  Applicants should have a strong aptitude for numbers and be proficient in tools like MS Excel, PowerPoint, Canva, and website management. The work location is the Faculty’s Cyberport campus. Flexibility to work overtime or on weekends when required is expected. The appointee will support the Faculty’s EMBA Marketing Team in planning, developing and implementing marketing strategies, social media contents and events for brand promotion.  Key Responsibilities include but not limited to: • planning, implementing and executing marketing strategies across different platforms, including LinkedIn, Google, WeChat, RedNote etc; • maintaining website and promotional collateral content to ensure all materials are up-to-date, while staying informed about the latest digital marketing trends, technologies and best practices; • working independently with vendors on event planning and execution, including script preparations, photo & video-related preparation, coordination, implementation and delivery; • coordinating with various stakeholders to support finance-related matters and overseas trips; and • supporting ad-hoc projects and other duties assigned by the Faculty. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537474 Manager, EMBA Marketing (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 15, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Glob