    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537491/part-time-research-assistant-i-ii": {
      "title": "Part Time Research Assistant I / II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Education 1 Part Time Research Assistant I / II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537491 Work type: Hourly-paid Department: Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part-time Research Assistant I / II in the Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (Ref.: 537491). To commence as soon as possible for 12 months. Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant I / II in the Centre for Information Technology in Education (CITE), Faculty of Education, to work on the project Longitudinal Research of Learning in the Digital World, funded by The Hong Kong Jockey Club Charities Trust and carried out in partnership with the OECD. The project is developing and validating an assessment of digital literacy for Primary 4 to Secondary 3 students across Hong Kong schools, with data collected annually over several years. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will • liaise with participating schools to arrange assessment sessions, and support the consent process with teachers and parents; • administer computer-based assessment sessions in schools and supervise student participants; • manage assessment and questionnaire data, including cleaning, coding, documentation and secure storage under the approved ethics protocol; • assist with statistical and psychometric analyses, and with the preparation of reports, presentations and publications; • assist with the development, translation and review of assessment tasks and questionnaires; and • carry out other duties assigned by the Principal Investigator. Requirements Applicants should have • a bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, statistics, computer science or a related field; a master’s degree is an advantage; • competence in a data-analysis environment such as R or Python; • a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese for work in schools; • strong organisational skills and attention to detail; and • the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Experience in educational assessment, psychometrics, school-based research or work with primary and secondary schools is an advantage. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 15, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537497/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537509/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537509 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow (3 posts) in Intelligent Transportation Systems in the Department of Civil Engineering (Ref.: 537509) We now invite applications for the captioned posts to work on the TIASim project , which aims to develop a Hong Kong-localised microscopic traffic simulation and visual analytics platform for Traffic Impact Assessment (TIA). Duties and Responsibilities The appointees will conduct research and development in one or more of the following areas: Develop, calibrate and validate microscopic traffic simulation models for Hong Kong traffic conditions; Develop Web-based transportation analysis and TIA workflow modules, including network editing, traffic demand configuration, scenario generation and mitigation assessment; Develop intelligent traffic diagnosis and mitigation scheme generation and evaluation methods; Develop transportation databases and AI-assisted workflows for traffic data and TIA report extraction, standardisation, validation and management; Analyse real-world transportation data, including traffic surveys, CCTV observations, vehicle trajectories and related datasets; Integrate traffic simulation, Web-based systems, transportation data and database modules; Conduct representative Hong Kong case studies for system validation and evaluation; and Prepare research publications, technical reports and project deliverables. Enquiries about the duties of the post should also be sent to Dr. Jintao Ke at kejintao@hku.hk. Descriptions of Dr. Ke can be found at https://sites.google.com/view/kejintao . Requirements Candidates should possess a Ph.D. degree in Transportation Engineering, Civil Engineering, Computer Science, Data Science, Operations Research, Applied Mathematics, Automation, or a related field. The following qualifications and experience are preferred: A strong research background in transportation modelling, traffic simulation, intelligent transportation systems, transportation data analytics, AI/machine learning, Web-based transportation systems, or database development; Strong programming skills in Python, C++, MATLAB, Java, JavaScript, R, or related languages; Experience in analysing real-world transportation data or developing transportation-related models/software; Strong analytical, communication and academic writing skills; and Ability to conduct independent research and work effectively in a multidisciplinary team. The project manpower plan requires the postdoctoral fellows to work full-time on the project. What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible for 1 or 2 year(s), depending on the duties and experience of the successful candidates, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post(s). Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537509 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537509 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537344/parttime-student-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Part-time Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Part-time Student Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537344 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part-time Student Research Assistant in the Department of Civil Engineering (Ref.: 537344), to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal. We now invite applications for the captioned post.  The successful candidate will primarily assist the research team in conducting field tests of a multimodal recommendation application developed by the research team. This position is open to current undergraduate students of HKU only .  We are looking for candidates who are patient, responsible, communicative, and able to commit sufficient time to fieldwork. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will work closely with PhD students and postdoctoral researchers in the research team.  The main duties include: Accompanying research team members to elderly care homes, community centres, and other relevant organisations to conduct field tests. Assisting elderly participants and other users in testing the multimodal recommendation application developed by the research team. Explaining the application and testing procedures to participants in Cantonese and Mandarin. Communicating patiently with elderly participants and providing assistance while they use the application. Collecting user feedback, survey responses, and other research data during field tests. Recording issues encountered by participants and reporting them to the research team. Assisting with the coordination and organisation of field-testing activities. Supporting other research-related tasks as assigned by the research team. Enquiries about the post should also be sent to Dr. Bin ZHOU at binchou@hku.hk . Requirements Applicants must be current undergraduate students of HKU and able to work on a part-time basis. The successful candidate should possess the following qualifications and attributes: Fluency in both Cantonese and Mandarin is essential. Patience and a willingness to communicate with elderly participants. A responsible, friendly, and respectful attitude. Good interpersonal and communication skills. Sufficient availability and flexibility to participate in field visits. Willingness to travel to elderly care homes, community centres, and other field-testing locations. Ability to follow research protocols and handle participant information responsibly. Ability to work effectively with PhD students, postdoctoral researchers, and other members of the research team. Undergraduate students from any academic discipline are welcome to apply.  Previous experience in volunteering, elderly care, community service, user studies, surveys, interviews, or field research would be an advantage but is not required. Programming and application development skills are not primary requirements .  Basic technical knowledge or an interest in mobile applications, artificial intelligence, transportation, or recommendation systems would be an advantage. W hat We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary part-time basis with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537344 Part-time Student Research Assistant Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537344 Part-time Student Research Assistant Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537511/research-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537511 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II (4 posts) in the Department of Civil Engineering (Ref.: 537511) , to commence as soon as possible for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. We now invite applications for the captioned posts to work on TIASim, a Hong Kong-localised microscopic traffic simulation platform for Traffic Impact Assessment (TIA). Duties and Responsibilities Support the development, calibration and validation of the TIASim microscopic traffic simulation engine; Support the development and testing of Web-based TIA workflow modules and the user interface; Assist with TIA report data extraction, database development, data checking and version management; and Assist in developing, testing and evaluating traffic diagnosis and mitigation measures. The appointees will also assist with Hong Kong traffic data analysis, software integration, case studies and project deliverables. Enquiries about the duties of the posts should also be sent to Dr. Jintao Ke at kejintao@hku.hk. Descriptions of Dr. Ke can be found at https://sites.google.com/view/kejintao . Requirements Candidates should possess a master’s degree in Computer Science, Transportation Engineering, Civil Engineering, Data Science or a related field. They must be able to commit to full-time employment without concurrent employment obligations. The following skills and knowledge are expected: Strong programming skills in Python, C++, Java or JavaScript; Knowledge of traffic simulation, transportation data analysis, artificial intelligence, Web development or database systems; and Good analytical skills and the ability to work effectively with researchers from different disciplines. MSc students at a Hong Kong University are also encouraged to apply and can be appointed as a part-time research assistant. What We Offer The appointments will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online through the University’s Careers site and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2027 or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537511 Research Assistant II Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537511 Research Assistant II Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Dec 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
