    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537454/lecturer-in-the-division-of-community-medicine-and-public-health-practice-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Lecturer in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Lecturer in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537454 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537454), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess an EdD or PhD or Master’s degree in public/global health or a related discipline such as exercise science; or MBBS with a specialist qualification in Public Health Medicine or equivalent. They should have at least 5 years’ teaching experience. They should be highly conversant with contemporary issues in public health, competent in case-based and problem-based teaching pedagogy, and able to work in an interdisciplinary and multicultural environment. High proficiency in English, enthusiasm in teaching, and good mentoring skills are essential. They should demonstrate a strong commitment to and evidence of excellence in teaching at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. A portfolio of programme administration, curriculum design and delivery, production of teaching materials, supervision of teaching practice, quality assurance, and/or student supervision is highly preferred. The appointee is expected to teach courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels in nursing leadership, public health, global health and development, evidence-based practice research, and business skills.  The appointee will contribute to the School’s knowledge exchange and community engagement initiatives, and perform other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV together with a teaching statement of no more than 2 pages.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537454 Lecturer in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537454 Lecturer in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537089/assistant-director-senior-manager-translational-research-and-commercialisation-at-the-rank-of-assistant-registrar-administrative-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537089 Work type: Full-time Department: Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) in the Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (RISE) (Ref.: 537089) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The University seeks a high-calibre, experienced professional to join us as Assistant Director/ Senior Manager, supporting translational research and commercialisation initiatives for the University and its subsidiaries, including R&D centres and partnership programmes, both locally and internationally. The appointee will develop strategic initiatives to advance translational research and commercialisation, leveraging the University’s strengths in life sciences to develop valuable IP assets, formulate commercialisation strategies, and build key partnerships and new ventures. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Vice-President (Research and Innovation) or their delegate and work collaboratively with faculties, units and subsidiaries across the University to foster a vibrant culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. Key Responsibility Develop and implement strategic initiatives to advance translational research, innovation, and commercialisation across the University and its subsidiaries, including R&D centres and partnership programmes. Identify, assess, and support high-potential technologies and research outcomes, providing guidance on intellectual property protection, development pathways, and commercialisation opportunities. Collaborate closely with academic faculties, researchers, innovators, and industry partners to accelerate the translation of research into societal and economic impact. Establish and strengthen strategic partnerships with industry, investors, regulators, government agencies, and international collaborators to create new opportunities for research translation and innovation. Negotiate and manage complex agreements related to research collaborations, intellectual property, licensing, venture creation, and strategic partnerships. Foster a vibrant innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystem by supporting incubation, acceleration, mentorship, and innovation programmes across the University. Promote the University's technology portfolio, innovation capabilities, and research strengths to industry leaders, investors, venture capital firms, and strategic partners globally. Qualifications and Qualities Possess a postgraduate degree, preferably a PhD, in a STEM, biomedical, healthcare, engineering, or related discipline; additional qualifications in business, innovation management, entrepreneurship, or intellectual property would be an advantage. Have at least 10 years of relevant experience in translational research, technology transfer, research commercialisation, business development, entrepreneurship, and venture investment, particularly within the life sciences or related fields. Demonstrate a successful track record of translating research outcomes into commercial or societal impact through licensing, startup formation, industry partnerships, or investment activities. Possess strong knowledge of intellectual property management, technology transfer, innovation ecosystems, and commercialisation practices. Have substantial experience in developing and managing collaborations with researchers, industry partners, investors, government agencies, and international stakeholders. Possess excellent communication, negotiation, stakeholder management, and relationship-building skills. Have experience working in Mainland China and international markets, with an understanding of global innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems. Be highly self-motivated, proactive, results-oriented, and capable of managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Possess an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua Applicants with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for appointment as Senior Manager. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided, where applicable, for the position of Assistant Director. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's career site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ), and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 14, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537089 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537089 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537376/fellowship-in-the-society-of-fellows-in-the-humanities": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537376 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Arts (04000) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Society of Fellows in the Humanities, Faculty of Arts The Society of Fellows in the Humanities aims to attract exceptional early-career postdoctoral scholars from around the world to Asia's global university. Located in one of the world's most dynamic cities and on Mainland China's doorstep, the University of Hong Kong offers unique opportunities to engage in cutting-edge research through its commitment to innovation and interdisciplinarity. The Faculty of Arts is one of HKU’s oldest and largest faculties and is consistently recognized as first in Asia for the Arts and Humanities. Its international outlook is reflected in the incredible diversity of its staff and students and its collaborations with other top universities around the globe. Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities (Ref.: 537376 ) The Society seeks outstanding applicants (appointed at the rank of Research Assistant Professor), with a flexible commencement date between June and August 2027 for a period of three years. The Society aims to establish a vibrant research community where Fellows interact with each other and other members of the Faculty.  Fellows will be expected to teach two courses during the term of their appointment and are required to submit a brief annual summary of their activities and accomplishments. The University of Hong Kong is an English-medium university. A host department within the Faculty of Arts will be selected on the basis of a Fellow’s proposed area of research. Applicants must have a PhD conferred after January 1, 2025, but not later than June 30, 2027. They will not be currently employed in tenure-track positions. A highly competitive package including medical benefits, annual leave, and conference and research support will be offered to the successful applicants. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. Applicants should apply online through the University’s careers website ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV, cover letter (not exceeding 300 words), research proposal (not exceeding 1500 words), and writing sample. They should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent directly by the referees to the Society at sofhku@hku.hk . Please refer to the Society of Fellows website ( https://www.sof.arts.hku.hk ) for the requirements for application documents and other details. Application will be reviewed by a panel of scholars from across the spectrum of the arts and the humanities. The application process closes on December 15, 2026 . Successful applicants will be notified by the end of February 2027. The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expresslyencourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537376 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities Faculty of Arts (04000) Dec 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537376 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities Faculty of Arts (04000) Dec 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
