    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537481/senior-clinical-practitionerclinical-practitioner-in-oral-and-maxillofacial-radiology": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537481 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537481), to commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for up to nine months. For appointment as Senior Clinical Practitioner , applicants must possess a dental or medical (Bachelor’s) degree or equivalent and a clinical specialist status in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology or equivalent.  Their clinical expertise should enjoy regional acclaim as evidenced by extensive clinical or teaching experience, regional clinical publications/presentations, and regional recognition of clinical excellence in a clinical specialty. For appointment as Clinical Practitioner , applicants must possess a dental or medical (Bachelor’s) degree or equivalent, demonstrate sound clinical experience and have a good track record of continuing professional education or formal advanced education such as an MDS degree or equivalent. The appointee will deliver clinical teaching to undergraduate students, provide clinical service, and manage patients.  He/She may be considered for appointment as a Senior Clinical Practitioner if registered as a specialist and may also provide clinical training to postgraduate students.  Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Professor C. McGrath at mcgrathc@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The successful candidate is required to obtain a valid registration with the Dental Council of Hong Kong.  (Note: Applicants who do not hold a local dental license must fulfil the essential requirements under the laws of a jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, China, in order to be eligible for Limited Registration.  For details, please refer to the Dental Council of Hong Kong’s website at https://www.dchk.org.hk/en/registration/part_III.html .) The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  They should also indicate clearly which post (i.e. Senior Clinical Practitioner or Clinical Practitioner) they wish to be considered for and please note that the final decision will be made by the University.  Closes October 29, 2026 . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537481 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537481 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
