    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537540/executive-assistant-undergraduate-student-enrichment-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537540 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537540) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a bachelor's degree, with at least 1to 2 years' full-time work experience in the field of administration or student affairs. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (proficiency in Putonghua would be an advantage); strong organisational, communication and problem-solving skills; computer literacy; and the ability to multitask under pressure and work independently as well as in a team. Attention to details, particularly with numerical data, is essential. Fresh graduates with a good academic background will also be considered. The appointee will provide administrative and clerical support to the Faculty’s undergraduate enrichment programmes. Duties include, but are not limited to, coordinating events, activities, and study tours; maintaining databases; liaising with students and internal/external stakeholders; performing data entry; and supporting general administration within the Undergraduate Student Enrichment Team. The appointee is expected to work outside normal office hours, travel occasionally, and perform ad hoc duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537540 Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537540 Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
