    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537541/it-technician": {
      "title": "IT Technician",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 IT Technician The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537541 Work type: Full-time Department: The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong IT Technician in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention within the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537541) Applications are invited for appointment as IT Technician in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention, Faculty of Social Sciences, to commence as soon as possible, on a temporary basis for up to one year, with University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, and with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Duties and Responsibilities Provide day-to-day technical support to Centre staff and assist in resolving IT-related issues; Assist in the maintenance of IT systems, platforms and equipment used for data collection and project implementation; Support the procurement, setup, inventory management and maintenance of IT equipment; Assist in liaising with vendors on system support, survey platforms, website maintenance and other IT-related services; Provide support for website updates, database maintenance, data storage, data security and server-related matters; Assist in IT project implementation, including system upgrades, data migration, web application testing and user support; Help maintain procedures, guidelines and documentation relating to data management and IT security; Provide technical support for research projects, events and meetings when needed; and Perform other ad-hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Diploma or above, preferably a Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science or a related discipline; Relevant work experience in IT support, system maintenance, web support, database management or related areas; Knowledge of computer hardware, software, networking, web applications and database systems; Experience in website maintenance, survey systems, data management, server support and/or IT equipment procurement would be an advantage; Experience in photography, photo editing, and/or video editing is advantageous; Relevant work experience in the higher education sector, preferably in a university setting, would be a definite advantage; Good problem-solving skills and the ability to provide timely technical support; Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain technical matters to non-technical users; A responsible, detail-minded and service-oriented attitude; The ability to work independently and as part of a team; and A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and written test. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a temporary basis for up to one year, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme will be provided. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits, where applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 3 0 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537541 IT Technician The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537541 IT Technician The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537546/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537546 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Surgery Applicants are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow under Department of Surgery, to commence as soon as possible for up to two years, with the possibility of renewal. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in biomedical engineering, biomedical sciences, bioengineering, materials science, or a related discipline, with experience in hydrogel biomaterials, cell culture, tissue engineering, or 3D bioprinting. The appointee should be organized, self-motivated, and able to work independently as well as in a team. The appointee will be involved in hydrogel bio-ink development, cell-laden and multicellular 3D bioprinting, vascularized tissue-model construction, cell culture, and biological and mechanical characterization of engineered constructs. Experience in rheology, confocal microscopy, immunofluorescence staining, SEM, mechanical testing, and image analysis will be an advantage. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V., including a full publication list. Review of applications will start from September 30, 2026 and review of applications will start on (2 weeks after posting) and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Successful applicants with satisfactory performance will have opportunities to publish in international journals, participate in international academic conferences, and contribute to collaborative research, technology transfer, and patent development. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  and continue until October 31,2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537546 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537546 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537553/assistant-human-resources-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Human Resources Officer",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Assistant Human Resources Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537553 Work type: Full-time Department: Human Resources Office (62000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Human Resources Officer in the Human Resources Office (HRO) (Ref.: 537553) We are looking for an Assistant Human Resources Officer to join the Human Resources Office to provide quality HR services to the University community. The Role The appointee will provide administrative support to a wide range of human resource functions (in the areas of employee relations and the development and review of HR policies), participate in various projects, and undertake other duties as assigned.  Training and development opportunities will be provided. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor’s degree, with at least 1 year’s relevant work experience; A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Putonghua); Good interpersonal and organisational skills, and IT proficiency; Prior HR experience is an advantage but not a must. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 30, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537553 Assistant Human Resources Officer Human Resources Office (62000) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537553 Assistant Human Resources Officer Human Resources Office (62000) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537501/clerical-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerical Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerical Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537501 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerical Assistant in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537501) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should have completed Form 5 or above.  They should have a fair command of English and Chinese, knowledge of MS Office applications, good telephone manners, as well as good communication and interpersonal skills.  The appointee is expected to provide general clerical support to the administrative office of the School, including attending counter and telephone enquiries, performing data entry, preparing meeting documents, copying and filing, etc.  He/She may be required to work outside normal office hours and on weekends.  Relevant work experience would be an advantage.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start on October 15, 2026 and continue until November 26, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537501 Clerical Assistant School of Nursing (20800) Nov 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537501 Clerical Assistant School of Nursing (20800) Nov 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
