    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537554/research-assistant-iii-in-the-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537554 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537554) (to commence as soon as possible for 12 months, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should preferably possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in nursing, psychology, public health, social sciences, statistics, data science, or other healthcare- or research-related disciplines. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and/or Putonghua), as well as good interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. They should be responsible, detail-oriented, and able to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team. Relevant experience in maternal and child health, sleep research, longitudinal or cohort studies, participant recruitment and follow-up, behavioral or video-based research, wearable or digital health technologies, and/or quantitative data analysis would be an advantage. Proficiency in statistical software or programming languages such as R, Python, SPSS, or Stata would also be desirable. Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for the post of Research Assistant II. The appointee will work under the supervision of Dr. Ying Dai on research projects in maternal and child sleep health supported by funding schemes including the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), the Research Grants Council General Research Fund (GRF), and other local and institutional funding schemes. Duties include participant recruitment and follow-up, data and sample collection, data management and analysis, behavioral/video coding, literature review, preparation of reports and manuscripts, coordination with research partners, and other research-related tasks as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31 , 202 6 , or until the post is filled, whichever is the earlier Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537554 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537554 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537529/executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537529 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537529) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years’ administrative experience, preferably in a tertiary institution, or a healthcare related field. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; strong communication, interpersonal, organizational and problem-solving skills; the ability to work independently and under pressure to meet tight deadlines; as well as an appropriate level of IT skills. Knowledge of design software would be an advantage. Applicants should also be self-motivated with a strong sense of responsibility, a good team player, capable of multitasking, and attentive to detail. The appointee will be responsible for the day-to-day operations and management, including but not limited to human resources, finance, research administration, managing social media platforms and marketing materials. They may also be assigned other duties as necessary. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from 9 October 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537529 Executive Officer Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537529 Executive Officer Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
