    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537177/professor-in-the-school-of-future-media": {
      "title": "Professor in the School of Future Media",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Professor in the School of Future Media Ref.: 537177 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Future Media (31200) Categories: Professoriate Staff Applications and nominations are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Professor in the School of Future Media (Ref.: 537177), to commence in Summer 2027 or from as soon as possible thereafter. School of Future Media The School of Future Media (SFM) at The University of Hong Kong (HKU) is a newly established interdisciplinary school dedicated to advancing education, research and creative practice at the intersection of journalism, documentary filmmaking, artificial intelligence and the global creative industries. Established in October 2025, the School brings together HKU’s Journalism and Media Studies Centre (JMSC), the Division of Documentary and AI Filmmaking, and the Division of Global Creative Industries, creating a distinctive platform for innovation across factual storytelling, screen-based media and emerging creative technologies. Building on the longstanding strengths of JMSC in journalism education and multimedia storytelling, SFM promotes an integrated approach spanning the humanities, creative arts and technology. It aims to prepare the next generation of storytellers, scholars and creators through interdisciplinary collaboration, ethical inquiry and engagement with the evolving media landscape in Hong Kong, the region and internationally. SFM offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate and research postgraduate programmes for a new generation of media professionals, creative practitioners and scholars. Current offerings include Bachelor of Journalism, Media and Artificial Intelligence, Bachelor of Arts in Global Creative Industries, Master of Journalism, Master of Journalism (Documentary Filmmaking Specialisation), Master of Arts in Creative Artificial Intelligence Film and Media, and a rigorous and interdisciplinary MPhil/PhD programme designed for aspiring scholars in journalism, media and communication studies. For more information about the School, please visit https://hkums.hku.hk/ . The Position The position is open to all areas in one or more of the following or related fields, including but not limited to: AI and generative AI in filmmaking Animation and game design Immersive and interactive media Computer vision Data journalism, data analytics, & technologies Business and finance journalism Digital humanities AI applications in journalism practices Entrepreneurship and innovation Global creative industries with expertise in one or more of the following areas: gaming and digital humanities, visual arts, heritage and museum studies, cultural industries, performing arts, visual communications. Duties and Responsibilities The appointees are expected to contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching and curriculum development, supervise postgraduate students, conduct high-quality research, and undertake administrative duties at SFM. Requirements A Ph.D. degree in film production and film studies, journalism and media studies, computer science, artificial intelligence, data science, and related fields; A strong commitment to excellence in research, teaching and mentoring; A proven track record in academic leadership and university-level administration; A distinguished and sustained record of conducting high-quality impactful research from publications, competitive grants and international recognition for scholarship; Strong connections and exposure in media industry or partners in China and/or Asia-Pacific region; Ability to establish strategic partnerships with industry and international academic institutions for fundraising, resource development and School’s advancement. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. Nomination, Expression of Interest and Application Applications from, and nominations of, individuals from diverse backgrounds are welcome, particularly those who are interested in contributing to the diversity and growth of the School of Future Media. Nominations, expressions of interest and applications should be directed in confidence to Heidrick & Struggles via email at hkusfm@heidrick.com . Review of nominations and applications will begin immediately and continue until the post is filled. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537177 Professor in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537177 Professor in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537462/research-assistant-professor-postdoctoral-fellow-in-mechanical-engineering": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537462 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Professional & Management Hong Kong Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering (Ref:537462 ) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities Carrying out research works under supervision for projects ranging from fundamental fluid dynamics and interfacial phenomena to biomedical and other applications Driving research activities towards defined goals in specified timeline Translating research to users through commercialization activities Processing in data analysis and management Drafting proposals, reports and presentations relevant to the projects Liaising with project collaborators and partners Performing various laboratory administrative duties Handling other relevant tasks as assigned by the supervisor(s) Requirements A PhD degree in Chemical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering / Mechanical Engineering / Chemistry or related engineering fields Relevant hands-on experience in microfluidics and diagnostic tool design is highly preferred Fresh graduates with outstanding academic achievement and strong passion in applied research of biomedical instrumentation will also be considered as Research Assistant Fluent in English in both writing and verbal communications; clear and concise writing skills Good time management with a strong sense of responsibility and research ethics Self-motivated team player who can be assertive to achieve results, and able to work under pressure What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 30, 2026 the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537462 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537462 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
